cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (below) and the paper listed under preferred-citation."
title: "Predicting Fungal Contaminants for Space Missions: proteome-wide ortholog screening pipeline"
abstract: >-
  A scalable, automated Python pipeline for identifying fungi with adaptation
  potential to spaceflight-associated stress conditions and pathogenicity risks.
  The pipeline extracts proteomes from UniProt, NCBI, JGI GOLD, and OrthoDB, runs
  BLASTp comparisons against reference sets of 25 stress-resistance proteins,
  summarizes results into identity-based S-score and A-score measures, annotates
  each organism with its taxonomic phylum, and generates the analytical matrices
  and visualizations presented in the accompanying paper.
